From 2d1a48287c73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elad Yifee <eladwf@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Jul 2024 18:29:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: use PP exclusively for XDP programs

PP allocations and XDP code path traversal are unnecessary
when no XDP program is loaded.
Prevent that by simply not creating the pool.
This change boosts driver performance for this use case,
allowing the CPU to handle about 13% more packets/sec.

Adapted to the 6.18 tree state (page pool creation guarded by
ring->buf_size <= MTK_PP_MAX_BUF_SIZE with a jumbo fallback):
the rcu_access_pointer() check is applied to both the pool
creation condition and the jumbo fallback, so the fallback
messages are not spammed when XDP is intentionally disabled.

Signed-off-by: Elad Yifee <eladwf@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: SmartWRT <smartwrt@localhost>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -3150,7 +3150,7 @@ static int mtk_rx_alloc(struct mtk_eth *eth, int ring_no, int rx_flag)
 	if (!ring->data)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	if (mtk_page_pool_enabled(eth) &&
+	if (mtk_page_pool_enabled(eth) && rcu_access_pointer(eth->prog) &&
 	    ring->buf_size <= MTK_PP_MAX_BUF_SIZE) {
 		struct page_pool *pp;
 
@@ -3160,7 +3160,7 @@ static int mtk_rx_alloc(struct mtk_eth *eth, int ring_no, int rx_flag)
 			return PTR_ERR(pp);
 
 		ring->page_pool = pp;
-	} else if (mtk_page_pool_enabled(eth)) {
+	} else if (mtk_page_pool_enabled(eth) && rcu_access_pointer(eth->prog)) {
 		if (rx_flag == MTK_RX_FLAGS_NORMAL && !ring_no && eth->netdev[0])
 			netdev_info(eth->netdev[0],
 				    "jumbo-rx: disable page_pool ring=%d buf_size=%d limit=%lu\n",
-- 
2.34.1
